  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason—probabilities of favorable outcomes and the treatment of outcome differences as negligible—aligns with what the individual considered. The individual focused on the higher probability in one lottery (0.2% vs 0.1%) and used this as the main justification, explicitly downplaying the small absolute difference in probability. This matches the rule of the decision reason, which prefers the lottery with the higher probability of a favorable outcome when outcome differences are negligible. The individual’s justification mirrors this logic, emphasizing probability as the decisive factor. Therefore, the decision reason appears to fully describe the individual’s deliberation process.",
